        <referenceFunction amount="1" category="electronics" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="This dataset can be applied to describe the entire production of a logic type integrated circuit. The included wafer fabrication data refers to a 200-mm wafer for a 32 MB DRAM chip, whereas the chip packaging data describes the material contents (in percent) of a plastic ball grid array package (PBGA) microchip (years 2002 to 2004). In 2023, the dataset is updated using the technical parameters found in the report of (Umweltbundesamt, 2021). This update mainly relates the energy and heat consumption, as well as the gold input for ICs. After consulting various reports and literature, it is decided that the mass flow of gold is unchanged, 0.0108 kg gold/kg packaged IC. The regionalization to the datasets is applied for the Eastern Asia electricity mix and global average, primary metal flows. The amount of wafer required (m2) to produce 1 kg IC is taken from the empirical study of (Teehan &amp; Kandlikar, 2013), which is 0.02 m2/kg packaged IC..; UUID: b9cb8b9e-539f-32ec-b096-046f3582e4df" includedProcesses="Describes all the processes required to produce a logic type microchip. Included are 'die separation', 'encapsulation', 'die attachment', 'lead bonding', 'plating', and 'marking'. These operations are represented by the material input of glass epoxy, metals, epoxy resin, doped silicon, glue, gold (wires) etc. and the assembly process energy used.The required the infrastructure, and the ship, train and road transport are also inventoried. Calculated for 1 kg of packaged logic IC." infrastructureIncluded="false" infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="electronics" localName="Integrated circuit, IC, logic type, at plant" localSubCategory="component" name="Integrated circuit, IC, logic type, at plant" subCategory="component" unit="kg">
